      "message": "So before we have a network request, the interface is set if the group extra is non-null\n\nBut after we have a request, it\u0027s when it\u0027s non-null and p2pInfo.groupFormed\u003d\u003dtrue\n\nBecause the \"getInterface\" logic is duplicated here, both cases need to be manually kept in sync, so there can be differences.\n\nInstead you could do:\n\n```\nfinal String newP2pIface \u003d getWifiP2pInterface(intent);\n\nif (!mMonitoringSockets || !hasAllNetworksRequests()) {\n    mWifiP2pTetherInterface \u003d newP2pIface;\n    return;\n}\n\nif (Objects.equals(mWifiP2pTetherInterface, newP2pIface)) return;\n\nif (mWifiP2pTetherInterface !\u003d null) {\n    // Remove the socket. Consider Log.wtf if newP2pIface is non-null (changed from\n    // interface A to B without null broadcast)\n}\n\nif (newP2pIface !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 !socketAlreadyExists) {\n    // Add the new socket\n}\n\n[...]\n\n@Nullable\nString getWifiP2pInterface(Intent intent) {\n    null group -\u003e null\n    null p2pInfo -\u003e null\n    !p2pInfo.groupFormed -\u003e null\n    else group.getInterface() (possibly null too ?)\n}\n```",
